  "latestPeriod": "2026-05 (financial year)",
  "coverage": "The Centre's gross fiscal deficit month by month, and the running total since April, ₹ crore, April 1994 on",
  "note": "RBI, Month-wise Gross Fiscal Deficit of the Central Government (DBIE report 349; Handbook), from the Controller General of Accounts. A negative month is a surplus (the RBI's dividend to the government usually lands in May). March is from the final accounts, so a year's twelve months add up to the year's accounts in the Centre's deficit table: checked, they do in 28 of 31 years; in 2012-13, 2013-14, 2017-18 the months differ from the year's audited figure by up to 1.1% (the monthly table was not restated). The running total is computed here."
